    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "u3aqw90",
      "content": "Heredity is the transmission of traits from parents to offspring. Genetics is the branch of biology that deals with the study of heredity and variation. Gregor Johann Mendel is known as the Father of Genetics."
    },
    {
      "id": "rtlcuq2",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Basic Genetic Terminology"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ltzk7jn",
      "content": "In genetics, specific terms are used to describe inheritance patterns. Understanding these terms is essential before studying Mendel’s laws."
    },
    {
      "id": "4sjldt0",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Term</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Meaning</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Gene</p>",
            "<p>Unit of heredity located on chromosome</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Allele</p>",
            "<p>Alternative form of a gene</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Trait</p>",
            "<p>Observable characteristic</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Genotype</p>",
            "<p>Genetic makeup of organism</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Phenotype</p>",
            "<p>Physical expression of trait</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3h640hn",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "twn0xv3",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3. Mendel and His Experiments"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "g4x3ame",
      "content": "Mendel conducted experiments on pea plants (Pisum sativum). He studied seven contrasting traits and established fundamental laws of inheritance."
    },
    {
      "id": "j9nxdwd",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4. Mendel’s Law of Dominance"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "89obo72",
      "content": "When two contrasting traits are present together, only one trait appears in F1 generation. The trait that appears is called dominant, while the hidden trait is recessive."
    },
    {
      "id": "htwuv1e",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5. Mendel’s Law of Segregation"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "00d0s5c",
      "content": "Alleles separate during gamete formation so that each gamete carries only one allele for each trait."
    },
    {
      "id": "umokcp0",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6. Mendel’s Law of Independent Assortment"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yglb1k6",
      "content": "Genes for different traits are inherited independently of one another when located on different chromosomes."
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "CHAPTER 8: HEREDITY & GENETICS",
      "id": "p6tcd7v"
    },
    {
      "id": "17g6qmy",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7. Dominant & Recessive Traits"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wfii7jk",
      "content": "Dominant traits are expressed even if only one allele is present. Recessive traits are expressed only when both alleles are recessive. "
    },
    {
      "id": "5kc5e9v",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Trait</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Type</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Tall (T)</p>",
            "<p>Dominant</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Dwarf (t)</p>",
            "<p>Recessive</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
